<!-- Worked answer for exercise 8: exercises/sigma/suspicious-curl.yml translated by hand
     into a Wazuh rule. Try the translation yourself before reading this.

     There is no Wazuh backend for sigma-cli (`sigma plugin list` has ~35 backends and
     Wazuh is not one of them), so for Wazuh the translation is always manual. What
     sigma-cli buys you here is the *field taxonomy check* — `sigma check`, and a
     reference query in a language that does have a backend.

     Note what the taxonomy costs you. Sigma's process_creation category has structured
     Image and CommandLine fields. Wazuh's auditd decoder exposes only audit.type and
     audit.id as fields; a0/a1/a2 stay in the raw message. So the structured Sigma
     match becomes a regex over the raw line. That lossiness is normal and is why you
     validate the translated rule instead of assuming it. -->
<group name="sigma,audit,">
  <rule id="100300" level="12">
    <if_sid>80700</if_sid>
    <regex type="pcre2">a\d+="[^"]*\b(?:curl|wget)"[\s\S]*(?:/tmp/|/dev/shm/|/var/tmp/|\|\s*(?:sh|bash))</regex>
    <description>Sigma T1105: curl/wget downloading into a drop directory</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1105</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>
</group>
